    "content": "Lockheed Martin has recently secured several major defense contracts, highlighted by a $4.76 billion US Army contract for PAC-3 missile production and a $4.1 billion missile defense award. Key deals include ramping up THAAD and PrSM missile production, alongside space-related technology upgrades. Major New Contracts (2026): PAC-3 Missile Segment Enhancement ($4.76B): Awarded by the US Army on April 9, 2026, for production, hardware, and technical support of interceptors through June 2030. THAAD Interceptor Production (Framework Agreement): Announced Jan 29, 2026, targeting to quadruple production to 400 interceptors per year. GPS IIIF Support ($105M): Awarded by Space Systems Command for GPS satellite launch and on-orbit testing support. Precision Strike Missile (PrSM) Acceleration: A new partnership with the Department of War to upgrade facilities and accelerate deliveries. Legion-ES Sensor Systems ($328.5M): Awarded for producing IRST21 sensor systems. Key Defense Partnerships: C2BMC System ($4.1B): Awarded by the Missile Defense Agency for developing and upgrading the Command and Control, Battle Management and Communications system. These contracts, many focusing on long-term production, are heavily driven by US Army demand and international sales, with significant work happening in Texas, Arkansas, and Alabama.",
